# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package version 2.0.0
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
Modified `app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the root layout body, placed after the existing `<Analytics />` component

The component was placed in the body of the root layout to ensure it tracks performance metrics across all pages of the application.

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
This project uses Next.js 16.2.7 with the App Router architecture, which is a modern Next.js version (13.5+). Following the official documentation, I used the `/next` import path for optimal integration with the App Router.

### Code Location
The SpeedInsights component was added to:
- **File**: `frontend/app/layout.tsx`
- **Location**: Inside the `<body>` tag, after the `<Analytics />` component
- **Import**: `@vercel/speed-insights/next` (Next.js-specific package)

### Placement Rationale
The component is placed in the root layout to ensure:
1. Speed metrics are collected from all pages in the application
2. The component is rendered once at the application root level
3. It follows the same pattern as the existing Vercel Analytics integration

## Verification Performed

✅ **Package Installation**: Successfully installed with npm
✅ **TypeScript Compilation**: Layout file compiles without errors
✅ **Linting**: No linting errors introduced in layout.tsx
✅ **Tests**: All 47 tests across 18 test files pass successfully
✅ **Lock Files**: package-lock.json properly updated with new dependencies

## Notes

- The Speed Insights component will automatically start collecting real user performance metrics when the application is deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration is required - the component works out of the box
- Data can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section after deployment
- The implementation follows the same pattern as the existing Vercel Analytics integration already present in the project

## Files Modified

1. `frontend/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component
2. `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
3. `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
